course: dictionary
lesson: 9337
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Spinning and weaving machines in big cotton mills made cloth much faster and cheaper, so ordinary people could afford more clothes.» Here spinning is not turning round. The clues are machines, mills and cloth, so spinning means making thread from fibres.
explain: Spinning can mean turning round quickly, making thread, or making silk. A spinning top turns round. A spider is spinning when it makes silk for its web. If your head is spinning, you feel dizzy or very confused. Always ask which meaning fits the clues around the word.
explain: «Spinning wheels with "win up to" prizes work like fruit machines, and most spins win small amounts.» Here spinning means the wheel turning round. The clues are prizes, wins and spins. Try your meaning in the sentence: does «turning round» fit? Yes, so it is right.
fact: Spinning means turning round and round quickly on the spot.
fact: Spinning also means making thread by twisting wool or cotton fibres, as people once did on a spinning wheel.
fact: «Spinning» is the -ing form of spin. Spin, spins, spun and spinning are all related.
fact: The Earth is spinning on its axis. One full spin takes about 24 hours, and this makes day and night.
fact: When you have many meanings, the context tells you which one to use.
exercise: «Spinning and weaving machines in big cotton mills made cloth much faster and cheaper.» What does spinning mean here? | *Making thread from cotton or wool fibres | Feeling dizzy | Turning round and round quickly on the spot | Dancing to music
exercise: Ella says, «My head is spinning after the fast ride.» What does spinning mean? | Sleeping well | *Feeling dizzy or very confused | Turning round on a bike | Making silk to build a web
exercise: «The spider was spinning a web in the corner.» What is the spider doing? | Sleeping | *Making silk to build a web | Hunting for food in the garden
test: «The spinning top wobbled and then fell over.» What does spinning mean? | *Turning round and round quickly | Feeling sick | Pedalling hard on a bike | Making thread
test: Which is a safety rule about spinning machines and fan blades? | Spin them faster to test them | *Keep fingers and hair away from them | Put your hand in to stop them
exam: «Spinning wheels with "win up to" prizes work like fruit machines.» In this sentence, spinning means | Making thread from fibres | Feeling dizzy | Making silk to build a web | *Turning round and round
